  ('cs_ariana-grande_sec3', 'ent_ariana-grande', 'narrative', 'Public image', 'Waxwork of Grande at Madame Tussauds , Bangkok Grande cited Audrey Hepburn as a major style influence in her early career; however, she later found emulating Hepburn''s style "a little boring". [ 398 ] She also drew inspiration from actresses of the 1950s and 1960s, such as Ann-Margret , Nancy Sinatra , and Marilyn Monroe . [ 398 ] Grande''s modest look early in her career was described as "age appropriate" in comparison to contemporary artists who grew up in the public eye. [ 387 ] Jim Farber of New York''s New York Daily News wrote in 2014 that Grande received less attention "for how little she wears or how graphically she moves than for how she sings." [ 399 ] That year, she abandoned her earlier style in favor of short skirts and crop tops with knee-high boots in live performances and red carpet events. [ 400 ] She also began regularly wearing cat and bunny ears and, subsequently, oversized jackets and hoodies through the late 2010s—the latter articles became largely associated with her persona. [ 401 ] [ 402 ] Grande later stated that owing to her mental health struggles at the time, she regularly wore variations of the oversized sweatshirt-boots outfit as she preferred to "hide away in something really cozy" and "did not have the mental energy to consider clothing". [ 403 ] Grande''s style is often imitated by social media influencers and celebrities. [ 404 ] [ 405 ] After years of dyeing her hair red for her role as Cat Valentine on Nickelodeon, Grande wore extensions as her hair recovered from damage. [ 406 ] Anne T. Donahue of MTV News noted that her "iconic" high ponytail has received more attention than her fashion choices. [ 407 ] Although Grande drew criticism for alleged impolite interactions with reporters and fans in 2014, [ 408 ] she dismissed the reports as "weird, inaccurate depictions". [ 3 ] Rolling Stone wrote: "Some may cry ''diva'', but it''s also Grande just taking a stand to not allow others to control her image." [ 409 ] In July 2015, Gran',
   '["clm_wiki_ariana-grande_sec3"]', '["src_wikidata"]',
   'general', 'en', 'assisted', 'kp-027-migration-0027', 'auto_approved', 1,
   80, unixepoch(), 'wikipedia', 353);
UPDATE content_section SET body_markdown = 'Arthur Robert Ashe Jr. was an American professional tennis player. He won three Grand Slam titles in singles and two in doubles. Ashe was the first Black player selected to the United States Davis Cup team, and the only Black man ever to win the singles titles at Wimbledon, the US Open, and the Australian Open. He retired in 1980.', word_count = 60, last_verified_at = unixepoch() WHERE id = 'cs_arthur-ashe_intro';
