  ('cs_bad-bunny_sec1', 'ent_bad-bunny', 'career', 'Music career', '2013–2019: Beginnings, X 100pre , and Oasis Main articles: X100pre and Oasis He started to write and create his own music at the age of 14. [ 24 ] In 2016, his song "Diles" caught the attention of DJ Luian from SoundCloud who signed him to his record label, Hear this Music. [ 3 ] [ 25 ] [ 26 ] His single " Soy Peor ", released in December 2016, reached number 19 on the Billboard Hot Latin Songs chart. [ 3 ] [ 27 ] In May 2017, his collaboration with Colombian singer Karol G , " Ahora Me Llama ", was released, reaching number 10 on the Billboard Hot Latin Songs chart. [ 28 ] [ 29 ] It was listed on "Alt.Latino''s Favorites: The Songs of 2017" as one of the best Latin songs of 2017. [ 29 ] In July 2017, Bad Bunny signed a booking deal with Cardenas Marketing Network (CMN) for several Latin American countries. [ 30 ] Bad Bunny in 2017 Starting in November 2017, Bad Bunny hosted Beats 1 ''s first Spanish-language show, Trap Kingz . [ 31 ] [ 32 ] The remix of " Te Boté " with Ozuna and Nicky Jam reached number one on the Hot Latin Songs chart. [ 33 ] In May 2018, American rapper Cardi B released a collaboration with Bad Bunny and J Balvin , " I Like It ", which topped the Billboard Hot 100 . [ 32 ] [ 34 ] On October 11, 2018, Bad Bunny released " Mia " with Drake , [ 35 ] [ 36 ] which reached number five on the Billboard Hot 100. [ 37 ] Bad Bunny released his debut album X 100pre on December 24, 2018, on the Rimas Entertainment label. [ 38 ] The album peaked at number 11 on the US Billboard 200 . [ 39 ] On Metacritic , X 100pre received an average score of 84 based on five reviews. [ 40 ] [ 41 ] Alexis Petridis of The Guardian praised Bad Bunny''s "off-kilter creativity". [ 41 ] In 2019, he was selected for the Forbes 30 under 30 list as an honoree in the Music category. [ 42 ] In 2020, X 100pre was voted 447th in Rolling Stone '' s 500 Greatest Albums of All Time . [ 43 ] On June 28, 2019, Bad Bunny released Oasis , an eight-song collaborative album with J Balvin. [ 44 ',
