  ('cs_ben-affleck_sec3', 'ent_ben-affleck', 'narrative', 'Politics', 'Political views Affleck has described himself as "moderately liberal ." [ 268 ] He was raised in "a very strong union household". [ 269 ] In 2000, he spoke at a rally at Harvard University in support of an increased living wage for all workers on campus; his father worked as a janitor at the university. [ 16 ] He later narrated a documentary, Occupation (2002), about a sit-in organized by the Harvard Living Wage Campaign. [ 270 ] Affleck and Senator Ted Kennedy held a press conference on Capitol Hill in 2004, pushing for an increase in the minimum wage . [ 271 ] He spoke at a 2007 press conference at Boston''s City Hall in support of SEIU ''s unionization efforts for the city''s low-paid hospital workers. [ 272 ] During the Writers'' Strike in 2008, Affleck voiced support for the picketers. [ 273 ] Affleck is pro-choice . In a 2000 interview, he stated that he believes "very strongly in a woman''s right to choose". [ 26 ] In 2012, he supported the Draw the Line campaign, describing reproductive rights as "fundamental". [ 274 ] Affleck was a longtime supporter of legalizing gay marriage , saying in 2004 that he hoped to look back on the marriage debate "with some degree of embarrassment for how antiquated it was". [ 275 ] Also that year, he remarked that it was "outrageous and offensive" to suggest members of the transgender community were not entitled to equal rights. [ 276 ] He appeared alongside his gay cousin in a 2005 Parents and Friends of Lesbians and Gays print advertising campaign. [ 277 ] In 2008, Affleck expressed concern about conspiracy theories claiming Barack Obama was an Arab or a Muslim : "This prejudice that we have allowed to fester in this campaign ... the acceptance of both of those things as a legitimate slur is really a problem." [ 278 ] [ 279 ] A reporter for The Washington Post overheard Affleck denouncing the Israeli invasion of Gaza at a Washington party in 2009. [ 280 ] Steven Clemons , a participant in the conversation, said Affleck liste',
