  ('cs_benny-hinn_sec2', 'ent_benny-hinn', 'narrative', 'Theology and practices', 'Hinn''s theology places strong emphasis on the anointing, which he claims is a divine empowerment capable of tangibly affecting bodies and being ministered through touch, gestures, or breath. Contemporary reporting has documented how this is expressed at his services: he has been observed blowing on attendees, rubbing or flicking his suit jacket toward the crowd, and making sweeping arm gestures, after which people fall or stagger, phenomena he attributes to the Holy Spirit ’s power. [ 24 ] Hinn cites healing evangelist Kathryn Kuhlman as a formative influence, linking his understanding of the Holy Spirit’s power and ministry style to her meetings and writings. [ 25 ] Slain in the Spirit Benny Hinn preaching at Jesus Image Church in 2025. Several attendees are seen lying on the floor after falling during a practice commonly described as being “slain in the Spirit.” A recurring feature of Hinn’s events is the phenomenon commonly called '' slaying in the Spirit ,'' in which participants fall backward, often into the arms of attendants (“catchers”), after prayer or physical contact on stage. [ 1 ] A 1987 report described a civil suit after an attendee was allegedly knocked into a bystander during a service where Hinn “was striking people on the forehead, claiming they were ‘slain of the spirit.’" [ 26 ] Scholars of religion and culture have analyzed such charismatic manifestations in broader charismatic contexts, variously interpreting them through lenses of embodiment, suggestion, ritual, and trance rather than exclusively supernatural causation. [ 27 ] Investigative writer Joe Nickell reported from a Hinn crusade that the responses resembled hypnotic suggestion and role-expectation, a view he contrasted with participants’ supernatural interpretations. [ 9 ] Faith healing Hinn frequently frames disease-curing miracles as central to his ministry. He identifies specific conditions—such as cancer, blindness, spinal ailments, and emotional afflictions—that prayer, touch, ',
   '["clm_wiki_benny-hinn_sec2"]', '["src_wikidata"]',
   'general', 'en', 'assisted', 'kp-027-migration-0027', 'auto_approved', 1,
   80, unixepoch(), 'wikipedia', 305);
