  ('cs_billy-joel_sec1', 'ent_billy-joel', 'career', 'Music career', '1964–1970: Early career Although Joel''s songs are infused with references to classical music , [ 42 ] his music mostly encompasses pop and rock , [ 43 ] fitting into the subgenres of pop rock [ 44 ] and soft rock . [ 45 ] Furthermore, Joel''s tightly structured melodies and down-to-earth songwriting betray the influence of early rock & roll and rhythm & blues artists, including Elvis Presley and the Everly Brothers . [ 46 ] After seeing the Beatles on The Ed Sullivan Show he decided to pursue a career in music. As he later commented: [ 47 ] .mw-parser-output .templatequote{overflow:hidden;margin:1em 0;padding:0 32px}.mw-parser-output .templatequotecite{line-height:1.5em;text-align:left;margin-top:0}@media(min-width:500px){.mw-parser-output .templatequotecite{padding-left:1.6em}} That one performance changed my life ... Up to that moment I''d never considered playing rock as a career ... (W)hen I saw four guys who didn''t look like they''d come out of the Hollywood star mill, who played their own songs and instruments, and especially because you could see this look in John Lennon ''s face—and he looked like he was always saying: ''---- you!''—I said: ''I know these guys, I can relate to these guys, I am these guys. This is what I''m going to do—play in a rock band''. At age 16, Joel joined the Echoes, [ 48 ] a group which specialized in British Invasion songs. The Echoes began recording in 1965. Joel played piano on several records released through Kama Sutra Productions and on recordings produced by Shadow Morton . He played on a demo version of " Leader of the Pack ", which in 1964 became a major hit for the Shangri-Las , [ 49 ] and has said that he was also on the demo or master recording of their song " Remember (Walking in the Sand) ". [ 50 ] The released single included a co-producer credit for Artie Ripp , [ 51 ] who later was the first to sign and produce Joel as a solo artist after Michael Lang , who had given Joel a monetary advance, passed Joel along to R',
