  ('cs_bruce-springsteen_sec2', 'ent_bruce-springsteen', 'legacy', 'Artistry and legacy', 'I spent most of my life as a musician measuring the distance between the American Dream and American reality. — Springsteen at a rally for presidential candidate Barack Obama on November 2, 2008 [ 265 ] Springsteen is one of the most acclaimed American rock performers in history. [ 266 ] Widely regarded as one of the greatest songwriters of all time, [ 267 ] Springsteen has been called a "rock ''n'' roll poet" who "[radiates] working-class authenticity". [ 268 ] He is considered a pioneer of heartland rock , a genre combining mainstream rock music with working class thematic concerns and socially conscious lyrics. According to Rolling Stone , his work "epitomizes rock''s deepest values: desire, the need for freedom and the search to find yourself." [ 269 ] Often described as cinematic in their scope, Springsteen''s lyrics frequently explore highly personal themes such as individual commitment, dissatisfaction and dismay with life in a context of everyday situations. [ 270 ] Springsteen''s themes include social and political commentary [ 271 ] [ 272 ] and are rooted in the struggles faced by his own family of origin. [ 273 ] A shift in Springsteen''s lyrical approach began with the album Darkness on the Edge of Town , [ 274 ] in which he focused on the emotional struggles of working class life, [ 275 ] [ 276 ] alongside more typical rock and roll themes. Reviewing Born in the U.S.A. , Rolling Stone critic Debby Miller noted that "Springsteen ignored the British Invasion and embraced instead the legacy of Phil Spector ''s releases, the sort of soul that was coming from Atlantic Records , and especially the garage bands that had anomalous radio hits. He''s always chased the utopian feeling of that music". [ 277 ] Despite his commercial success, Springsteen has remained grounded in his working-class roots throughout his career, which researchers at Penn State University say has contributed to his lasting impact. [ 278 ] Jon Pareles included Springsteen among the "panthe',
   '["clm_wiki_bruce-springsteen_sec2"]', '["src_wikidata"]',
