  ('cs_buster-keaton_sec2', 'ent_buster-keaton', 'narrative', 'Promotional and commercial films', 'Buster Keaton found steady work as an actor in TV commercials for Colgate, Alka-Seltzer, U.S. Steel, 7-Up, RCA Victor, Phillips 66, Milky Way, Ford Motors, Minit-Rub and Budweiser, among others. [ 73 ] In a series of pantomime television commercials for Simon Pure Beer made in 1962 by Jim Mohr in Buffalo, New York , Keaton revisited some of the gags from his silent-film days. [ 74 ] In 1961, Keaton appeared in promotional films for Maryvale , a housing development in the western part of Phoenix . [ 75 ] [ 76 ] [ 77 ] [ 78 ] [ 79 ] With Joe E. Brown in the 1962 Route 66 episode "Journey to Nineveh"',
