  ('cs_claude-shannon_sec1', 'ent_claude-shannon', 'narrative', 'The Mathematical Theory of Communication', 'Weaver''s Contribution Shannon''s The Mathematical Theory of Communication, [ 58 ] begins with an interpretation of his own work by Warren Weaver . Although Shannon''s entire work is about communication itself, Warren Weaver communicated his ideas in such a way that those not acclimated to complex theory and mathematics could comprehend the fundamental laws he put forth. The coupling of their unique communicational abilities and ideas generated the Shannon-Weaver model , although the mathematical and theoretical underpinnings emanate entirely from Shannon''s work after Weaver''s introduction. For the layman, Weaver''s introduction better communicates The Mathematical Theory of Communication , [ 105 ] but Shannon''s subsequent logic, mathematics, and expressive precision was responsible for defining the problem itself. [ citation needed ]',
