VALUES
  ('cs_conan-obrien_sec1', 'ent_conan-obrien', 'career', 'Career', 'Early writing jobs and Saturday Night Live (1985–1991) After graduating from Harvard, O''Brien moved to Los Angeles to join the writing staff of HBO ''s sketch comedy series Not Necessarily the News , where he worked for two seasons. [ 30 ] Around this time, he started taking improvisation classes with Cynthia Szigeti and The Groundlings . [ 31 ] [ 32 ] His next job as a writer was on the short-lived The Wilton North Report . [ 33 ] In January 1988, Saturday Night Live ( SNL ) executive producer Lorne Michaels hired O''Brien as a writer. [ 34 ] During his three years on SNL , he wrote such recurring sketches as "Mr. Short-Term memory" and "The Girl Watchers"; the latter was first performed by Tom Hanks and Jon Lovitz . [ 35 ] While on a writers'' strike from Saturday Night Live following the 1987–88 season, O''Brien put on an improvisational comedy revue in Chicago with fellow SNL writers Bob Odenkirk and Robert Smigel called Happy Happy Good Show . [ 36 ] [ 37 ] While living in Chicago, O''Brien briefly shared an apartment with Jeff Garlin near Wrigley Field . [ 38 ] In 1989, O''Brien and his fellow SNL writers received an Emmy Award for Outstanding Writing for a Variety Series . [ 39 ] O''Brien, like many SNL writers, occasionally appeared as an extra in sketches; his most notable appearance was as a doorman in a sketch in which Tom Hanks was inducted into the SNL " Five-Timers Club " for hosting his fifth episode in 1990. [ 40 ] O''Brien and Robert Smigel wrote the television pilot for Lookwell starring Adam West , which aired on NBC in 1991. [ 41 ] Even with support from NBC president Brandon Tartikoff , the pilot never went to series. [ 42 ] Despite the negative reviews, it became a cult hit . [ 43 ] It was later screened at The Other Network , a festival of unaired TV pilots produced by Un-Cabaret ; it featured an extended interview with O''Brien and was rerun in 2002 on the Trio network. [ 44 ] In 1991, after the failure of his sitcom, O''Brien also had an en',
   '["clm_wiki_conan-obrien_sec1"]', '["src_wikidata"]',
   'general', 'en', 'assisted', 'kp-027-migration-0027', 'auto_approved', 1,
