  ('cs_conan-obrien_sec2', 'ent_conan-obrien', 'career', 'Other work', 'Television production See also: Conaco O''Brien was executive producer and co-wrote the pilot of the 2007 NBC adventure/comedy series Andy Barker, P.I. , starring O''Brien''s sidekick Andy Richter . [ 177 ] After six episodes and low ratings, the show was canceled despite being named one of the Top Ten Shows of 2007 by Entertainment Weekly . [ 178 ] [ 179 ] Later, USA Network ordered a pilot episode of the medical-themed Operating Instructions , which was produced by O''Brien''s production company Conaco . [ 180 ] In January 2010, NBC ordered two pilots from Conaco, the one-hour courtroom drama Outlaw and a half-hour comedy. [ 181 ] Outlaw was produced in eight episodes and premiered on September 15, 2010. [ 182 ] Voice work O''Brien''s first guest appearance after beginning his late-night career was playing himself in the season five Simpsons episode " Bart Gets Famous ", interviewing Bart Simpson during his rise to fame as a catchphrase comedian. [ 49 ] In 1999, O''Brien made an appearance on Futurama in the second-season episode " Xmas Story ". O''Brien played himself as a head in a jar and still alive in the year 3000. [ 183 ] O''Brien has made multiple voice appearances on the Adult Swim series Robot Chicken , including the specials Robot Chicken: Star Wars and Robot Chicken: Star Wars Episode II . [ 184 ] Other voice work performed by O''Brien includes the voice of Robert Todd Lincoln in the audiobook version of Assassination Vacation by Sarah Vowell , [ 185 ] the voice of talk show host Dave Endochrine in the 2013 DC Universe Animated Original Movie Batman: The Dark Knight Returns (Part 2) , [ 186 ] the voice of the character Kuchikukan in the " Operation: Lunacorn Apocalypse " episode of Nickelodeon''s The Penguins of Madagascar , [ 187 ] and the voice of Santa Claus in The Backyardigans episode "The Action Elves Save Christmas Eve". [ 188 ] In 2026, O’Brien joined Disney ’s Toy Story universe as Smarty Pants in the fifth installment of the film series. [ 18',
   '["clm_wiki_conan-obrien_sec2"]', '["src_wikidata"]',
   'general', 'en', 'assisted', 'kp-027-migration-0027', 'auto_approved', 1,
