  ('cs_david-gilmour_sec1', 'ent_david-gilmour', 'career', 'Career', 'Pink Floyd In 1967, Pink Floyd , composed of Gilmour''s Cambridge schoolmates Barrett and Waters with Nick Mason and Richard Wright , released their debut studio album, The Piper at the Gates of Dawn . [ 18 ] That May, Gilmour briefly returned to London in search of new equipment. During his stay, he watched Pink Floyd record " See Emily Play " and was shocked to find that Barrett, who was suffering mental health problems, did not seem to recognise him. [ 19 ] Gilmour (left) performing with Pink Floyd in 1973 In December 1967, after Gilmour had returned to England, he accepted an invitation to join Pink Floyd to cover for the increasingly erratic Barrett. They initially intended to continue with Barrett as a non-performing songwriter. [ 20 ] One of the band''s business partners, Peter Jenner , said the plan was to have Gilmour "cover for Barrett''s eccentricities". [ 21 ] By March 1968, working with Barrett had become too difficult and he agreed to leave the band. [ 22 ] Mason later said: "After Syd, Dave was the difference between light and dark. He was absolutely into form and shape and he introduced that into the wilder numbers we''d created. We became far less difficult to enjoy, I think." [ 23 ] In 1970, Gilmour attended the Isle of Wight Festival and assisted in a live mix of a Jimi Hendrix performance. [ 24 ] Gilmour performing with Pink Floyd in the mid-1970s In the 1970s, Gilmour received a copy of a demo tape by the teenage songwriter Kate Bush from Ricky Hopper, a mutual friend of both families. Impressed, Gilmour paid for Bush, then 16, to record three professional demo tracks to present to record labels. [ 25 ] [ 26 ] The tape was produced by Gilmour''s friend Andrew Powell , who went on to produce Bush''s first two studio albums, and the sound engineer Geoff Emerick . [ 27 ] Gilmour arranged for EMI executive Terry Slater to hear the tape, [ 28 ] and Slater signed her. [ 29 ] Gilmour is credited as the executive producer on two tracks on Bush''s debut ',
   '["clm_wiki_david-gilmour_sec1"]', '["src_wikidata"]',
   'general', 'en', 'assisted', 'kp-027-migration-0027', 'auto_approved', 1,
