  ('cs_david-gilmour_sec3', 'ent_david-gilmour', 'legacy', 'Legacy and impact', 'According to MusicRadar , Gilmour is "a household name among the classic rock crowd, and for a lot of younger guitar fans he''s the only 1970s guitarist that matters. For many he''s the missing link between Jimi Hendrix and Eddie Van Halen." [ 97 ] The MusicRader writer Billy Saefong wrote that Gilmour "isn''t as flashy as Jimi Hendrix or Jimmy Page on the stage, but his guitar work outshines most for emotion." [ 131 ] In 1996, Gilmour was inducted into the Rock and Roll Hall of Fame as a member of Pink Floyd. He has been ranked one of the greatest guitarists of all time by publications including Rolling Stone [ 132 ] [ 133 ] and The Daily Telegraph . [ 134 ] In January 2007, Guitar World readers voted Gilmour''s solos for " Comfortably Numb ", " Time " and " Money " among the top 100 greatest guitar solos. [ 135 ] He was voted the 36th-greatest rock singer by Planet Rock listeners in 2009. [ 136 ] Rolling Stone named Gilmour the 14th-greatest guitarist of all time in 2011 [ 137 ] and the 28th-greatest guitarist in 2023. [ 5 ] Gilmour was cited by the Marillion guitarist Steve Rothery as one of his three main influences. [ 138 ] John Mitchell and the guitarists of bands It Bites and Arena also cite Gilmour as an influence. [ 139 ] In 2013, Gary Kemp , the guitarist and songwriter of Spandau Ballet and a member of Nick Mason''s Saucerful of Secrets , argued that Gilmour''s work on The Dark Side of the Moon "must make him the best guitar player in recent history". [ 140 ]',
   '["clm_wiki_david-gilmour_sec3"]', '["src_wikidata"]',
   'general', 'en', 'assisted', 'kp-027-migration-0027', 'auto_approved', 1,
   90, unixepoch(), 'wikipedia', 282);
UPDATE content_section SET body_markdown = 'David Michael Letterman is an American television host, comedian, writer, and producer. He hosted late-night television talk shows for 33 years, beginning with the February 1, 1982, debut of Late Night with David Letterman on NBC and ending with the May 20, 2015, broadcast of Late Show with David Letterman on CBS. In total, Letterman hosted 6,080 episodes of Late Night and Late Show, surpassing his friend and mentor Johnny Carson as the longest-serving late-night talk show host in American television history.', word_count = 82, last_verified_at = unixepoch() WHERE id = 'cs_david-letterman_intro';
