  ('cs_doja-cat_sec2', 'ent_doja-cat', 'narrative', 'Artistry', 'Influences Nicki Minaj has been cited as one of Doja Cat''s primary influences. Doja Cat has cited Nicki Minaj as one of her influences. [ 239 ] [ 240 ] In a Billboard interview, Doja Cat stated that she is "in love with everything Nicki Minaj has put out into the world". [ 241 ] On the song " Get Into It (Yuh) " from her third studio album, Planet Her (2021), she pays tribute to Minaj and borrows lyrics and rap delivery from her debut 2010 single " Massive Attack ". [ 242 ] [ 243 ] Critics noted that the album as a whole was largely influenced by Minaj, [ 244 ] [ 142 ] [ 245 ] with The New Yorker noting that she "build[s] upon the pop-rap legacy established by her predecessor". [ 246 ] She has also named Lauryn Hill and Busta Rhymes as some of her biggest influences. [ 247 ] [ 248 ] While speaking about Busta Rhymes, she stated: "if I hear a beat Busta Rhymes would absolutely kill, I''ll use my voice to do a flow similar to his." [ 70 ] Additionally, Doja Cat has cited Rihanna , [ 249 ] [ 51 ] Beyoncé , [ 250 ] [ 251 ] D''Angelo , [ 249 ] Missy Elliott , [ 252 ] Christina Aguilera , [ 253 ] Pharrell Williams , [ 254 ] and Lil'' Kim [ 255 ] as major influences. She draws inspiration from her background engaging in online activities and delving into subcultures as a suburban teenager, [ 45 ] as well as the artists her mother exposed to her as a child, such as Fugees , Erykah Badu , Jamiroquai , Earth, Wind & Fire , Black Eyed Peas , Seal , Tupac , Aaliyah , DMX , India Arie , and TLC . [ 70 ] [ 256 ] [ 36 ] The Hindu culture of her childhood as well as Japanese culture have also been noted as sources of inspiration for Purrr! (2014) and other aspects of her early career. [ 257 ] [ 258 ] In an interview with Big Boy , she stated her admiration for Janet Jackson and Prince . [ 251 ] In April 2026, Doja has publicly defended and expressed admiration for Madonna , specifically calling out ageist criticism against the pop legend. [ 259 ] Musical style Doja Cat''s music ha',
