  ('cs_doja-cat_sec3', 'ent_doja-cat', 'narrative', 'Public image', 'Doja Cat has been noted for being versatile in her music. This includes her ability to sing, rap , and produce , [ 260 ] [ 52 ] as well as perform and dance. [ 261 ] Often described as eccentric , [ 262 ] [ 263 ] [ 51 ] she is known for her absurdly humorous personality and posts on social media platforms. [ 264 ] [ 265 ] As one of the biggest and best-performing commercial artists of the 2020s decade, writers at Billboard expressed that "it''d be tough to name three artists of any kind who feel more like the 2020s so far than Doja Cat." [ 266 ] Bryan Rolli of Forbes wrote that "Doja Cat''s aloof, irreverent, chronically online persona masks a tireless work ethic; she sings better, raps faster and dances harder than many of her peers, all at once." [ 267 ] In an article for Okayplayer , Robyn Mowatt noted that "as a singer, rapper, songwriter, and entertainer Doja has led her fans on a rambunctious journey equipped with snappy lyrics, live video streams, outlandish outfits, and memorable viral moments. It''s not just the music that gets her fans riled up, it''s also her live performances which typically are infused with a touch of eccentricity." [ 268 ] Her extensive online presence and bold persona have at times garnered controversy. NME named her Milkshake Duck of the year in 2018 following public circulation of 2015 tweets in which she referred to other performers as " faggots ". [ 269 ] [ 270 ] After initially defending herself, she apologized and deleted the tweets. [ 271 ] She faced similar backlash for comments she made regarding the COVID-19 pandemic . [ 272 ] In 2022, public criticism of Doja Cat heightened when she did not come outside to greet fans waiting at a hotel, after her scheduled performance at Asunciónico was cancelled due to severe weather. [ 273 ] Frustrated with the backlash, Doja Cat announced she was quitting the music industry. After a brief Twitter hiatus, she retracted that statement. [ 274 ] She faced a similar fan response after a Threa',
