  ('cs_dustin-hoffman_sec1', 'ent_dustin-hoffman', 'career', 'Career', '1960–1966: Early theatre roles Hoffman''s first acting role was at the Pasadena Playhouse, alongside future Academy Award–winner Gene Hackman . [ 28 ] After two years there, Hackman headed for New York City, with Hoffman soon following. Hoffman, Hackman, and Robert Duvall lived together in the 1960s, whilst all three of them focused on finding acting jobs. [ 29 ] [ 30 ] Hackman remembers, "The idea that any of us would do well in films simply didn''t occur to us. We just wanted to work". [ 26 ] Hoffman''s appearance—Duvall described him as Barbra Streisand in drag—and small size made him uncastable, Vanity Fair later wrote. [ 31 ] During this period, Hoffman got occasional television bit parts, including commercials but, needing income, he briefly left acting in order to teach. Hoffman then studied at Actors Studio and became a dedicated method actor . In 1960 Hoffman was cast in a role in an off-Broadway production and followed with a bit part in his Broadway debut in production, A Cook for Mr. General (1961). [ 32 ] In 1962, he appeared in Rabbit Run Theatre''s summer stock production of Write Me a Murder in Madison, Ohio [ 33 ] and served as an assistant director to Ulu Grosbard on The Days and Nights of BeeBee Fenstermaker at off-Broadway''s Sheridan Square Playhouse . In 1964, Hoffman appeared in Three Men on a Horse at Princeton ''s McCarter Theatre [ 34 ] and in 1965, in off-Broadway''s Harry, Noon and Night [ 35 ] with Joel Grey . On June 23, 1965, he played Mendy in a practice run of Philip Roth ''s abandoned off-Broadway play The Nice Jewish Boy , directed by Gene Saks and co-starring Melinda Dillon . [ 36 ] [ 37 ] Grosbard and Hoffman reunited for a 1965 recording of Death of a Salesman starring Lee J. Cobb and Mildred Dunnock , with Hoffman playing Bernard. [ 38 ] He was assistant director for Grosbard''s 1965 off-Broadway production of A View from the Bridge starring Robert Duvall and Jon Voight , [ 39 ] and in late 1965 stage-managed and appeared in Gr',
   '["clm_wiki_dustin-hoffman_sec1"]', '["src_wikidata"]',
   'general', 'en', 'assisted', 'kp-027-migration-0027', 'auto_approved', 1,
   20, unixepoch(), 'wikipedia', 357);
