  ('cs_george-jones_sec3', 'ent_george-jones', 'narrative', 'Duets', 'Jones released many duets over the course of his career. While his songs with Tammy Wynette are his best known, Jones claimed in his autobiography that he felt his duets with Melba Montgomery were his best. Jones also recorded duet albums with Gene Pitney and his former bass player Johnny Paycheck . Jones also recorded the duet albums My Very Special Guests (1979), A Taste of Yesterday''s Wine with Merle Haggard (1982), Ladies Choice (1984), Friends In High Places (1991), The Bradley Barn Sessions (1994), God''s Country: George Jones And Friends (2006), a second album with Merle Haggard called Kickin'' Out The Footlights...Again (2006), and Burn Your Playhouse Down (2008).',
   '["clm_wiki_george-jones_sec3"]', '["src_wikidata"]',
   'general', 'en', 'assisted', 'kp-027-migration-0027', 'auto_approved', 1,
