  ('cs_george-w-bush_sec1', 'ent_george-w-bush', 'career', 'Career', 'Military career Main article: George W. Bush military service controversy See also: Killian documents controversy and Killian documents authenticity issues In May 1968, Bush joined the United States Air Force and was commissioned into the Texas Air National Guard . [ 17 ] After two years of training in active-duty service, [ 18 ] he was assigned to Houston , flying Convair F-102s with the 147th Reconnaissance Wing out of Ellington Field Joint Reserve Base . [ 17 ] [ 19 ] Critics, including former Democratic National Committee Chairman Terry McAuliffe , have alleged that Bush was favorably treated due to his father''s political standing as a member of the House of Representatives , citing his selection as a pilot despite his low pilot aptitude test scores and his irregular attendance. [ 17 ] In June 2005, the Department of Defense released all the records of Bush''s Texas Air National Guard service, which remain in its official archives. [ 20 ] In late 1972 and early 1973, he drilled with the 187th Fighter Wing of the Alabama Air National Guard . He had moved to Montgomery, Alabama , to work on the unsuccessful U.S. Senate campaign of Republican Winton M. Blount . [ 21 ] [ 22 ] In 1972, Bush was suspended from flying for failure to take a scheduled physical exam. [ 23 ] He was honorably discharged from the Air Force Reserve on November 21, 1974. [ 24 ] Bush remains the most recent president to have served in the military. [ 25 ] Business career Main article: Professional life of George W. Bush Bush with former president Gerald Ford in August 1984 In 1977, Bush established Arbusto Energy , a small oil exploration company, which began operations in 1978. [ 26 ] [ 27 ] He later changed the name to Bush Exploration. In 1984, his company merged with the larger Spectrum 7 , and Bush became chairman. The company was hurt by decreased oil prices, and it folded into Harken Energy Corporation , [ 28 ] with Bush becoming a member of Harken''s board of directors. Questions of po',
   '["clm_wiki_george-w-bush_sec1"]', '["src_wikidata"]',
