  ('cs_george-w-bush_sec3', 'ent_george-w-bush', 'career', 'Presidential campaigns', '2000 presidential campaign Main articles: George W. Bush 2000 presidential campaign , 2000 Republican Party presidential primaries , and 2000 United States presidential election Primary Bush portrayed himself as a compassionate conservative , implying he was more centrist than other Republicans. He campaigned on a platform which included bringing integrity and honor back to the White House, increasing the size of the military, cutting taxes, improving education, and aiding minorities. [ 39 ] By early 2000, the race had centered on Bush and Arizona senator John McCain . [ 39 ] Bush won the Iowa caucuses and, although heavily favored to win the New Hampshire primary , trailed McCain by 19% and lost. Despite this, he regained momentum and effectively became the front runner after the South Carolina primary , which according to The Boston Globe made history for his campaign''s negativity. The New York Times described it as a smear campaign . [ 62 ] [ 63 ] [ 64 ] General election On July 25, 2000, Bush surprised some observers when he selected Dick Cheney – a former White House chief of staff , U.S. representative, and secretary of defense – to be his running mate. At the time, Cheney was serving as head of Bush''s vice presidential search committee. Soon after at the 2000 Republican National Convention , Bush and Cheney were officially nominated by the Republican Party. [ 65 ] Bush continued to campaign across the country and touted his record as Governor of Texas. [ 39 ] During his campaign, Bush criticized his Democratic opponent, incumbent vice president Al Gore , over gun control and taxation. [ 66 ] When the election returns were tallied on November 7, Bush had won 29 states, including Florida. The closeness of the Florida outcome led to a recount . [ 39 ] The initial recount also went to Bush, but the outcome was tied up in lower courts for a month until eventually reaching the U.S. Supreme Court . [ 67 ] On December 9, in the controversial Bush v. Gore ruling, [ ',
   '["clm_wiki_george-w-bush_sec3"]', '["src_wikidata"]',
   'general', 'en', 'assisted', 'kp-027-migration-0027', 'auto_approved', 1,
   20, unixepoch(), 'wikipedia', 346);
UPDATE content_section SET body_markdown = 'George Washington was a Founding Father and the first president of the United States, serving from 1789 to 1797. As commander of the Continental Army, Washington led Patriot forces to victory in the American Revolutionary War against the British Empire. He is commonly known as the Father of His Country for his role in bringing about American independence.', word_count = 58, last_verified_at = unixepoch() WHERE id = 'cs_george-washington_intro';
