VALUES
  ('cs_grover-cleveland_sec1', 'ent_grover-cleveland', 'career', 'Political career in New York', 'Sheriff of Erie County A statue of Grover Cleveland outside City Hall in Buffalo, New York From his earliest involvement in politics, Cleveland aligned with the Democratic Party . [ 39 ] He had a decided aversion to Republicans John C. Frémont and Abraham Lincoln , and the heads of the Rogers law firm were solid Democrats. [ 40 ] In 1865, he ran for District Attorney , losing narrowly to his friend and roommate, Lyman K. Bass , the Republican nominee. [ 33 ] In 1870, with the help of friend Oscar Folsom, Cleveland secured the Democratic nomination for sheriff of Erie County, New York . [ 41 ] He won the election by a 303-vote margin and took office on January 1, 1871, at age 33. [ 42 ] [ 43 ] While this new career took him away from the practice of law, it was rewarding in other ways: the fees were said to yield up to $40,000, equivalent to $1,075,000 in 2025 , over the two-year term. [ 41 ] Cleveland''s service as sheriff was unremarkable. Biographer Rexford Tugwell described the time in office as a waste for Cleveland politically. Cleveland was aware of graft in the sheriff''s office during his tenure and chose not to confront it. [ 44 ] A notable incident of his term took place on September 6, 1872, when Patrick Morrissey was executed. He had been convicted of murdering his mother. [ 45 ] As sheriff, Cleveland was responsible for either personally carrying out the execution or paying a deputy $10 to perform the task. [ 45 ] In spite of reservations about the hanging, Cleveland executed Morrissey himself. [ 45 ] He hanged another murderer, John Gaffney , on February 14, 1873. [ 46 ] After his term as sheriff ended, Cleveland returned to his law practice, opening a firm with his friends Lyman K. Bass and Wilson S. Bissell . [ 47 ] Bass was later replaced by George J. Sicard . [ 48 ] Elected to Congress in 1872, Bass did not spend much time at the firm, but Cleveland and Bissell soon rose to the top of Buffalo''s legal community. [ 49 ] Up to that point, Cleveland''',
   '["clm_wiki_grover-cleveland_sec1"]', '["src_wikidata"]',
   'general', 'en', 'assisted', 'kp-027-migration-0027', 'auto_approved', 1,
   20, unixepoch(), 'wikipedia', 372);
