  ('cs_hank-aaron_sec2', 'ent_hank-aaron', 'career', 'Career overall', 'For his career, Aaron batted .305 with 3771 hits, including 624 doubles, 98 triples, and 755 home runs. In 17 postseason games, including two World Series (1957, ''58) and the 1969 NLCS, Aaron batted .362 (25-for-69) with 11 runs scored, 4 doubles, 1 triple, 6 home runs, 16 RBI, 5 walks, on-base percentage of .405, slugging percentage of .710, and on-base plus slugging percentage of 1.116. [ 1 ] Statistics and achievements More information Legend ... Legend Bold All-time leader Close More information Category, Years ... Category Years WAR G AB R H 2B 3B HR TB XBH RBI SB BB AVG OBP SLG OPS FLG% Reference "}]],"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"Abbr","href":"./Template:Abbr"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"Ref."},"2":{"wt":"Reference"}},"i":0}}]}">Ref. Total 23 143.2 3,298 12,364 2,174 3,771 624 98 755 6,856 1,477 2,297 240 1,402 .305 .374 .555 .928 .982 [ 1 ] Close',
