  ('cs_harry-styles_sec3', 'ent_harry-styles', 'narrative', 'Cultural status', 'Main article: Cultural impact of Harry Styles Styles on Love On Tour in 2022 Styles has been referred to as a pop icon , [ 215 ] [ 216 ] [ 217 ] a fashion icon , [ 218 ] [ 219 ] [ 220 ] and a global icon . [ 221 ] [ 222 ] [ 223 ] He is considered to be among the most successful solo artists to have emerged from a band. [ 224 ] [ 225 ] Ben Beaumont-Thomas of The Guardian wrote that he is "a star who has negotiated one of the most difficult transitions in music – from boyband to solo artist – with more panache than even successful forebears such as Justin Timberlake and Robbie Williams ". [ 226 ] In 2023, it was announced that Texas State University would be offering a course on Styles called "Harry Styles and the Cult of Celebrity: Identity, the Internet and European Pop Culture", analysing the relations of Styles''s career with "questions of gender and sexuality, race, class, nation and globalism, media, fashion, fan culture, internet culture and consumerism." [ 227 ] [ 228 ] In 2022, "As It Was" was the most-streamed song of the year globally on Spotify and Deezer , the second-most-streamed song globally on Apple Music, and the most-streamed song in the UK overall. [ 229 ] Forbes noted that with Harry''s House , Styles racked up a first-week vinyl sales count larger than anything any musician has managed before. [ 230 ] Styles was the second-most-searched musician on Google in 2022, after Taylor Swift. [ 231 ] Rolling Stone UK named Styles the "new King of Pop" in 2022, following his groundbreaking year. [ 232 ] [ 217 ] Styles''s fan base is known as "Harries". [ 233 ] Styles has inspired his fans to dress up for his concerts, leading Fashionista to call the shows "his fans'' Met Gala ". Outfits often include sequins, pink cowboy hats, and feather boas. [ 234 ] [ 235 ] Styles''s fans have been featured in Vogue , [ 236 ] The New York Times , [ 237 ] and The New Yorker . [ 238 ] Since One Direction''s early years, a group of shipping conspiracy theorist fans, often ',
