VALUES
  ('cs_hr-mcmaster_sec3', 'ent_hr-mcmaster', 'career', 'Post-military career', 'In September 2018, McMaster began work as a Bernard and Susan Liautaud Visiting Fellow at Stanford University ''s Freeman Spogli Institute for International Studies . [ 78 ] He was appointed to the Fouad and Michelle Ajami Senior Fellowship at Stanford''s Hoover Institution and serves as a lecturer in strategy at Stanford Graduate School of Business [ 79 ] effective September 1, 2018, as that institution had announced on July 2 that year. [ 80 ] In 2019, McMaster became an Advisory Board Member of Spirit of America , a 501(c)(3) organization that supports deployed US personnel. [ 81 ] In 2020, McMaster became a board member of Zoom Video Communications , [ 82 ] and advisor to Mischler Financial Group Inc . [ 83 ] He is Chairman of Ergo''s Flashpoints Forum, a consultancy firm. In 2021, McMaster joined the National Security Advisory Board of venture capital firm, Shield Capital, as Senior Advisor. [ 84 ] In September 2021, McMaster joined the advisory board of the geospatial-intelligence corporation Edgybees. [ 85 ] In January 2022, he joined the advisory board of Strider Technologies , [ 86 ] a software firm focused on economic statecraft risk vis-à-vis strategic competition with China. [ 87 ] In 2021 McMaster was appointed Distinguished University Fellow at Arizona State University [ 46 ] where he serves as a subject matter expert on national security and defense issues. Also serving as an Arizona State University guest lecturer, [ 88 ] he guides and mentors students, and hosts special events surrounding national security and defense to advance Arizona State University''s lead in competitive statecraft. In September 2021 McMaster was removed from the United States Military Academy ''s Board of Visitors by President Joe Biden as part of a mass removal of 18 Trump appointees [ 89 ] on the boards of the three service branches. [ 90 ] The Heritage Foundation deplored the purge; at the time it was thought that some of the 18 would contest the presidential decision in co',
