  ('cs_j-craig-venter_sec2', 'ent_j-craig-venter', 'narrative', 'Published books', 'Venter was the author of three books, the first of which is an autobiography titled A Life Decoded . [ 10 ] In Venter''s second book, Life at the Speed of Light , he announced his theory that this is the generation in which there appears to be a dovetailing of the two previously diverse fields of science represented by computer programming and the genetic programming of life by DNA sequencing. [ 71 ] He was applauded for his position on this by futurist Ray Kurzweil . Venter''s most recent book, co-authored by David Ewing Duncan , The Voyage of Sorcerer II: The Expedition that Unlocked the Secrets of the Ocean''s Microbiome , details the Global Ocean Sampling Expedition , spanning a 15-year period during which microbes from the world''s oceans were collected and their DNA sequenced. [ 72 ]',
   '["clm_wiki_j-craig-venter_sec2"]', '["src_wikidata"]',
   'general', 'en', 'assisted', 'kp-027-migration-0027', 'auto_approved', 1,
