  ('cs_james-taylor_sec3', 'ent_james-taylor', 'narrative', 'Personal life', 'Taylor performing with his first wife and fellow singer Carly Simon in 1975 Taylor and Smedvig in September 2008 Taylor married singer-songwriter Carly Simon on November 3, 1972, in a low-key ceremony at Simon''s home in New York. Taylor was 24 and Simon 29. [ a ] They divorced in 1983. [ 107 ] Their children, Sally and Ben, are also musicians. [ 108 ] Taylor married actress Kathryn Walker at the Cathedral of St. John the Divine on December 14, 1985. [ 109 ] She helped him fight his heroin addiction, but they divorced in 1996. [ 68 ] In 1995, Taylor began dating Caroline "Kim" Smedvig, the director of public relations and marketing for the Boston Symphony Orchestra . [ 110 ] They had met when he performed with the composer, John Williams and the Boston Pops orchestra. [ 110 ] They were married at the Emmanuel Episcopal Church in Boston on February 18, 2001. Part of their relationship was worked into the 2002 album October Road , specifically on the songs "On the 4th of July" and "Caroline I See You". [ 111 ] Following the birth of their twin sons Rufus and Henry in April 2001, [ 110 ] [ 112 ] they settled in Lenox, Massachusetts . [ 113 ] Their son Henry has toured as a backing vocalist with his father as of 2021. [ 114 ]',
