VALUES
  ('cs_jeff-bezos_sec2', 'ent_jeff-bezos', 'narrative', 'Public image', 'Bezos at a naturalization ceremony on June 14, 2016 Journalist Nellie Bowles of The New York Times has described the public persona and personality of Bezos as that of "a brilliant but mysterious and coldblooded corporate titan". [ 155 ] During the 1990s, Bezos earned a reputation for relentlessly pushing Amazon forward, often at the expense of public charity and social welfare. [ 155 ] [ 156 ] Journalist Mark O''Connell criticized Bezos''s relentless customer focus as "very small" in terms of impact on humanity as a whole, [ 157 ] a sentiment technologist Tim O''Reilly agreed with. [ 158 ] His business practices projected a public image of prudence and parsimony with his own wealth and that of Amazon. Throughout the early 2000s, he was perceived to be geeky or nerdy. [ 31 ] [ 159 ] [ 160 ] Bezos was seen by some as needlessly quantitative and data-driven. [ 161 ] [ 162 ] This perception was detailed by Alan Deutschman, who described him as "talking in lists" and "[enumerating] the criteria, in order of importance, for every decision he has made". [ 31 ] Select accounts of his persona have drawn controversy and public attention. Notably, journalist Brad Stone wrote a book that described Bezos as a demanding boss as well as hyper-competitive , [ 156 ] [ 161 ] and opined that Bezos perhaps "bet the biggest on the Internet" out of anyone. [ 163 ] Bezos has been characterized as a notoriously opportunistic CEO who operates with little concern for obstacles and externalities . [ 164 ] [ 165 ] During the early 2010s, Bezos solidified his reputation for aggressive business practices, and his public image began to shift. Bezos started to wear tailored clothing ; he weight trained , pursued a regimented diet and began to freely spend his money. [ 166 ] His physical transformation has been compared to the transformation of Amazon; he is often referred to as the metonym of the company. [ 167 ] [ 168 ] Since 2017, he has been portrayed by Kyle Mooney and Steve Carell on Saturda',
   '["clm_wiki_jeff-bezos_sec2"]', '["src_wikidata"]',
   'general', 'en', 'assisted', 'kp-027-migration-0027', 'auto_approved', 1,
   80, unixepoch(), 'wikipedia', 353);
