  ('cs_jerry-falwell_sec2', 'ent_jerry-falwell', 'career', 'Social and political views', 'Families Falwell advocated beliefs and practices influenced by his version of biblical teachings. [ vague ] [ 34 ] Tithing In 1989, he told Liberty University employees that membership in his church and tithing were mandatory. [ 35 ] Vietnam War Falwell felt the Vietnam War was being fought with "limited political objectives" when it should have been an all-out war against the North . [ 36 ] In general, Falwell held that the president "as a minister of God" has the right to use arms to "bring wrath upon those who would do evil." [ 37 ] Civil rights On his evangelist program The Old-Time Gospel Hour in the mid-1960s, Falwell regularly featured segregationist politicians like governors Lester Maddox and George Wallace . [ 38 ] Of Martin Luther King Jr. , he said: "I do question the sincerity and nonviolent intentions of some civil rights leaders such as Dr. Martin Luther King Jr., Mr. James Farmer, and others, who are known to have left-wing associations." [ 39 ] Of Brown v. Board of Education , he said in 1958: .mw-parser-output .templatequote{overflow:hidden;margin:1em 0;padding:0 32px}.mw-parser-output .templatequotecite{line-height:1.5em;text-align:left;margin-top:0}@media(min-width:500px){.mw-parser-output .templatequotecite{padding-left:1.6em}} If Chief Justice Warren and his associates had known God''s word and had desired to do the Lord''s will, I am quite confident that the 1954 decision would never have been made. The facilities should be separate. When God has drawn a line of distinction, we should not attempt to cross that line. [ 40 ] In 1977, Falwell supported Anita Bryant ''s " Save Our Children " campaign to overturn an ordinance in Dade County, Florida , prohibiting discrimination on the basis of sexual orientation . He supported a similar movement in California. [ 4 ] Twenty-eight years later, during a 2005 MSNBC television appearance, Falwell said he was not troubled by reports that the nominee for Chief Justice of the United States Supreme Court, J',
   '["clm_wiki_jerry-falwell_sec2"]', '["src_wikidata"]',
   'general', 'en', 'assisted', 'kp-027-migration-0027', 'auto_approved', 1,
