  ('cs_jerry-rice_sec1', 'ent_jerry-rice', 'career', 'College career', 'Rice attended Mississippi Valley State University from 1981 to 1984. [ 35 ] When Rice arrived at Mississippi Valley State, he attended summer school and freshman orientation before the regular season. Two of his former teammates from B.L. Moor were there as well, but both left before the start of training camp. [ 36 ] Rice studied receiving techniques from Gloster Richardson , stating: "I soaked up everything I could." [ 37 ] Rice with the Mississippi Valley State Delta Devils in 1983 In 1981, Rice''s freshman season, he caught 30 passes for 428 yards and two touchdowns. [ 38 ] In 1982, his sophomore year, Rice played his first season with freshman quarterback Willie Totten . [ 39 ] They became friends and practiced into the evening. [ 40 ] Under the direction of Cooley, Mississippi Valley State ran an "unusual" offense, playing four wide receivers who tended to line up on one side of the field. [ 41 ] Rice caught 66 passes for 1,133 yards and seven touchdowns. [ 42 ] Together, Totten and Rice became known as "The Satellite Express." [ 40 ] Success on the field did not put any money in his pocket, and many times he relied on friends for food, stating that the food given to him at Mississippi Valley "were not enough for a growing man". [ 43 ] Rice had a record-setting 1983 campaign, including NCAA marks for receptions (102) and receiving yards (1,450). He was named a first-team Division I-AA All-American . [ 44 ] He set a single-game NCAA record with 24 receptions against Southern University . He acquired the nickname "World," because of his ability to seemingly catch anything thrown near him. [ 39 ] After an August practice experiment, Cooley had Totten call all the plays at the line of scrimmage without a huddle , resulting in even more staggering offensive numbers. [ 41 ] Rice caught 17 receptions for 199 yards against Southern, 17 receptions for 294 yards, and five receiving touchdowns against Kentucky State , and 15 for 285 yards against Jackson State . [ 45 ] [',
   '["clm_wiki_jerry-rice_sec1"]', '["src_wikidata"]',
   'general', 'en', 'assisted', 'kp-027-migration-0027', 'auto_approved', 1,
