  ('cs_jesse-jackson_sec2', 'ent_jesse-jackson', 'narrative', 'LGBT rights activism', 'Jackson was an ardent advocate and early supporter of LGBT rights in the United States . While seeking the 1984 Democratic presidential nomination , he became the first person to mention gays and lesbians in a major-party convention speech when he included gays and lesbians as part of the fabric of American society in his speech to the 1984 Democratic National Convention , saying, "the lesbian, the gay [...] make up the American quilt" and "The rainbow includes lesbians and gays. No American citizen ought to be denied equal protection from the law". [ 42 ] In 1987, while seeking the 1988 Democratic presidential nomination , Jackson was one of the leaders of the Second National March on Washington for Lesbian and Gay Rights . [ 42 ] In both of his presidential campaigns, Jackson placed LGBT rights front and center in a way no presidential candidate had done before, advocating for ending employment discrimination against gay employees and for ending the ban on openly gay service members in the military . [ 42 ] [ 43 ] In 1993, he spoke at the March on Washington for Lesbian, Gay, and Bi Equal Rights and Liberation , saying: "No more homophobia. Let''s respect people, protect people. Everyone is somebody". [ 42 ] In 2004, Jackson spoke out in support of same-sex marriage in a speech in Massachusetts , which had become the first state to recognize same-sex marriage , saying, "Gays deserve the right of choice to choose their own partners". [ 42 ] In 2010, he gave a speech to a gay rights rally in San Francisco at the United States Court of Appeals for the Ninth Circuit , [ 42 ] which was then considering a case challenging 2008 California Proposition 8 , [ 44 ] and said: .mw-parser-output .templatequote{overflow:hidden;margin:1em 0;padding:0 32px}.mw-parser-output .templatequotecite{line-height:1.5em;text-align:left;margin-top:0}@media(min-width:500px){.mw-parser-output .templatequotecite{padding-left:1.6em}} We stand with you today to support marriage equality and to de',
   '["clm_wiki_jesse-jackson_sec2"]', '["src_wikidata"]',
   'general', 'en', 'assisted', 'kp-027-migration-0027', 'auto_approved', 1,
   80, unixepoch(), 'wikipedia', 318);
