VALUES
  ('cs_joe-dimaggio_sec3', 'ent_joe-dimaggio', 'narrative', 'Marriages', 'Dorothy Arnold In January 1937, DiMaggio met actress Dorothy Arnold on the set of Manhattan Merry-Go-Round , in which he had a minor role, and she was an extra. He announced their engagement on April 25, 1939, just before the Yankees were to meet the Philadelphia Athletics . [ 48 ] They married at Saints Peter and Paul Church, San Francisco on November 19, 1939, as 20,000 well-wishers jammed the streets. The couple''s son, Joseph Paul DiMaggio Jr. (1941–1999), was born at Doctors'' Hospital in Staten Island. [ 49 ] Their marriage was troubled, as Arnold wanted DiMaggio to settle down and be a father to their son and a nearby husband to her; DiMaggio was more interested in the public eye. [ 50 ] The couple divorced in 1944, while DiMaggio was on leave from the Yankees during World War II. [ citation needed ] Marilyn Monroe DiMaggio with wife Marilyn Monroe , January 1954 According to her autobiography My Story , co-written with Ben Hecht , [ 51 ] American actress Marilyn Monroe originally did not want to meet DiMaggio, fearing he was a stereotypical arrogant athlete. However, they did meet in Los Angeles while on a blind date . [ 52 ] After dating for two years, [ 53 ] they eloped at San Francisco City Hall on January 14, 1954. [ 52 ] Although she suffered from endometriosis , Monroe and DiMaggio each expressed to reporters their desire to start a family. [ 54 ] The union was troubled from the start by DiMaggio''s jealousy, controlling attitude, and him physically abusing Monroe, [ 55 ] as well as her busy life as an actress. [ 54 ] A violent fight entailing physical assault between the couple occurred immediately after Monroe filmed the skirt-blowing scene in The Seven Year Itch that was filmed on September 14, 1954, in front of Manhattan''s Trans-Lux 52nd Street Theater, as DiMaggio disapproved of the scene. [ 56 ] Then 20th Century Fox ''s East Coast correspondent Bill Kobrin told the Palm Springs Desert Sun that it was director Billy Wilder ''s idea to turn the s',
   '["clm_wiki_joe-dimaggio_sec3"]', '["src_wikidata"]',
