  ('cs_john-coltrane_sec3', 'ent_john-coltrane', 'narrative', 'Veneration', 'Main article: St. John Coltrane African Orthodox Church Quick facts Saint, Venerated in ... Saint John Coltrane Coltrane icon at the St. John Coltrane African Orthodox Church Venerated in African Orthodox Church Episcopal Church [ citation needed ] Canonized 1982, St. John Coltrane Church, 2097 Turk Blvd, San Francisco , California, 94115, by the African Orthodox Church [ 114 ] Feast December 8 (AOC) Patronage All artists Close After Coltrane''s death, a congregation called the Yardbird Temple in San Francisco began worshipping him as God incarnate. [ 115 ] The group was named after Charlie "Yardbird" Parker , whom they equated to John the Baptist . [ 115 ] The congregation became affiliated with the African Orthodox Church ; this involved changing Coltrane''s status from a god to a saint. [ 115 ] The resultant St. John Coltrane African Orthodox Church in San Francisco is the only African Orthodox church that incorporates Coltrane''s music and his lyrics as prayers in its liturgy. [ 116 ] Rev. F. W. King, describing the African Orthodox Church of Saint John Coltrane, stated, "We are Coltrane-conscious ... God dwells in the musical majesty of his sounds." [ 117 ] For The New York Times , journalist Samuel G. Freedman wrote, .mw-parser-output .templatequote{overflow:hidden;margin:1em 0;padding:0 32px}.mw-parser-output .templatequotecite{line-height:1.5em;text-align:left;margin-top:0}@media(min-width:500px){.mw-parser-output .templatequotecite{padding-left:1.6em}} ... the Coltrane church is not a gimmick or a forced alloy of nightclub music and ethereal faith. Its message of deliverance through divine sound is actually quite consistent with Coltrane''s own experience and message. ... In both implicit and explicit ways, Coltrane also functioned as a religious figure. Addicted to heroin in the 1950s, he quit cold turkey, and later explained that he had heard the voice of God during his anguishing withdrawal. ... In 1966, an interviewer in Japan asked Coltrane what he hop',
   '["clm_wiki_john-coltrane_sec3"]', '["src_wikidata"]',
