  ('cs_john-f-kennedy_sec2', 'ent_john-f-kennedy', 'narrative', 'Journalism (1945)', 'In April 1945, Kennedy''s father, who was a friend of William Randolph Hearst , arranged a position for his son as a special correspondent for Hearst Newspapers ; the assignment kept Kennedy''s name in the public eye and "expose[d] him to journalism as a possible career". [ 72 ] He covered the United Nations Conference on International Organization in San Francisco , the British elections , and the Potsdam Conference in Germany. [ 73 ]',
