  ('cs_john-steinbeck_sec3', 'ent_john-steinbeck', 'legacy', 'Death', 'The Steinbeck family graves in the Hamilton plot at the Salinas Cemetery John Steinbeck died in New York City, where his writing career had begun, on December 20, 1968, during the 1968 flu pandemic of heart disease and congestive heart failure . He was 66, and had been a lifelong smoker. An autopsy showed nearly complete occlusion of the main coronary arteries . [ 23 ] In accordance with his wishes, his body was cremated, and interred on March 4, 1969 [ 60 ] at the Hamilton family gravesite in Salinas, with those of his parents and maternal grandparents. His third wife, Elaine, was buried in the plot in 2004. He had written to his doctor that he felt deeply "in his flesh" that he would not survive his physical death, and that the biological end of his life was the final end to it. [ 36 ] Steinbeck''s incomplete novel based on the King Arthur legends of Malory and others, The Acts of King Arthur and His Noble Knights , was published in 1976.',
   '["clm_wiki_john-steinbeck_sec3"]', '["src_wikidata"]',
   'general', 'en', 'assisted', 'kp-027-migration-0027', 'auto_approved', 1,
