  ('cs_julia-roberts_sec2', 'ent_julia-roberts', 'narrative', 'Other ventures', 'Philanthropy Roberts has contributed to UNICEF as well as other charitable organizations. Her six-day visit to Port-au-Prince , Haiti in 1995, as she said, "to educate myself", [ 140 ] [ 141 ] was expected to trigger an outburst of donations—$10 million in aid was sought at the time—by UNICEF officials. [ 140 ] [ 141 ] In 2006, she became a spokeswoman for Earth Biofuels as well as chair of the company''s newly formed advisory board promoting the use of renewable fuels. [ 142 ] In 2013, she was part of a Gucci campaign, "Chime for Change", that aims to spread female empowerment. [ 143 ] In 2000, Roberts narrated a documentary about Rett syndrome , a neurodevelopmental disorder, [ 144 ] designed to help raise public awareness about the disease, and in 2014, she was the voice of Mother Nature in a short film for the Conservation International campaign Nature Is Speaking , intended to raise awareness about climate change . [ 145 ] Production company Roberts runs the production company Red Om Films (Red Om is "Moder" spelled backwards, after her husband''s last name [ 146 ] ) with her sister, Lisa Roberts Gillan, and Marisa Yeres Gill. [ 147 ] Through Red Om, Roberts has served as an executive producer for various projects she has starred in such as Eat Pray Love and Homecoming , as well as for the first four films of the American Girl film series (based on the American Girl line of dolls), released between 2004 and 2008. Endorsements In 2006, Roberts signed an endorsement deal with fashion label Gianfranco Ferre , valued at $6 million. She was photographed by Mario Testino in Los Angeles for the brand''s advertising campaign, which was distributed in Europe , Asia and Australia . [ 148 ] Since 2009, Roberts has acted as Lancôme ''s global ambassador, a role in which she has been involved in the development and promotion of the brand''s range of cosmetics and beauty products. [ 149 ] She initially signed a five-year extension with the company for $50 million in 2010. [ ',
   '["clm_wiki_julia-roberts_sec2"]', '["src_wikidata"]',
   'general', 'en', 'assisted', 'kp-027-migration-0027', 'auto_approved', 1,
