  ('cs_julia-roberts_sec3', 'ent_julia-roberts', 'narrative', 'Artistry', 'Acting style and reception Throughout her career, Roberts has frequently been referred to as " America''s sweetheart " by the media, [ 153 ] [ 154 ] [ 155 ] a label that Vogue writer Noor Brara linked to her portrayals of characters that embody elements of the trope. [ 156 ] BBC News Online attributed her early popularity to her roles as relatable, girl-next-door characters, [ 153 ] often portraying vulnerable working-class women. [ 157 ] Geoffrey Macnab of The Independent noted that during her peak, Roberts''s appeal stemmed from her ability to blend the glamour of classic Hollywood stars with an approachable, down-to-earth quality. [ 158 ] While romantic comedies cemented her status as an international star, Erin Brockovich is often cited as the film that earned her broader critical recognition as an actress. [ 153 ] [ 159 ] [ 160 ] Film critic David Edelstein observed that while Roberts is widely acknowledged as a movie star, critics and cinephiles have debated the extent of her acting abilities, sometimes discussing her work with a degree of skepticism. [ 157 ] [ 160 ] In 2012, HuffPost writer Mike Ryan suggested that her career has relied more on her star power than on widespread acclaim for her acting, noting that she is not often included in discussions of the industry''s most celebrated actresses. [ 161 ] Some critics have pointed out that Roberts has frequently played characters with traits similar to her own, [ 160 ] [ 162 ] contributing to a screen presence that journalist and filmmaker Bilge Ebiri described as difficult to separate from her public persona. [ 163 ] John Anderson of The Seattle Times described her as "an actress who has never really been required to act". [ 162 ] Matt Singer of The Dissolve said "Roberts has rarely strayed far from the onscreen persona that made her one of the biggest movie stars in history—that of a simple girl of limited means and unlimited heart, pulling herself up by her bootstraps". [ 160 ] Attempts to divert from thi',
   '["clm_wiki_julia-roberts_sec3"]', '["src_wikidata"]',
   'general', 'en', 'assisted', 'kp-027-migration-0027', 'auto_approved', 1,
   80, unixepoch(), 'wikipedia', 347);
UPDATE content_section SET body_markdown = 'Justin Drew Bieber is a Canadian singer. Regarded as a prominent figure in contemporary popular music, he rose to fame in the late 2000s after being discovered by American talent manager Scooter Braun, who signed him to Raymond Braun Media Group (RBMG). Bieber subsequently released his debut extended play, My World (2009), receiving international recognition and establishing himself as a teen idol.', word_count = 62, last_verified_at = unixepoch() WHERE id = 'cs_justin-bieber_intro';
