  ('cs_justin-bieber_sec3', 'ent_justin-bieber', 'narrative', 'Achievements', 'Main article: List of awards and nominations received by Justin Bieber Queen Elizabeth II Diamond Jubilee Medal Throughout his career, Bieber has sold an estimated 150 million records worldwide, making him one of the best-selling music artists of all time . [ 256 ] [ 257 ] In 2011, Bieber was honoured with a star in front of Avon Theater in Stratford, Ontario , Canada, where he used to busk when he was younger. On November 23, 2012, Bieber was presented with the Queen Elizabeth II Diamond Jubilee Medal by the former Prime Minister of Canada, Stephen Harper . He was one of 60,000 Canadians to receive the Diamond Jubilee medal that year. [ 258 ] In 2013, Bieber received a Diamond award from the Recording Industry Association of America (RIAA) for his single " Baby ", which at the time became the highest-certified digital single of all time . [ 259 ] [ 260 ] Bieber is credited with five Diamond certifications from the RIAA. [ 10 ] Bieber has won two Grammy Awards out of 23 nominations, [ 261 ] one Latin Grammy Award , [ 262 ] eight Juno Awards , [ 263 ] two Brit Awards , [ 264 ] [ 265 ] 26 Billboard Music Awards , [ 266 ] 19 American Music Awards , [ 267 ] 22 MTV Europe Music Awards (the most wins for any artist), [ 268 ] 23 Teen Choice Awards (the most wins for a male individual), [ 269 ] eight iHeartRadio Music Awards , and six MTV Video Music Awards . At age 19, Bieber received the Milestone Award at the 2013 Billboard Music Awards in recognition for breaking boundaries with his creativity and contribution to the musical landscape. [ 270 ] [ 271 ] As of 2024, all of Bieber''s studio projects are certified Platinum or higher by the RIAA and have received numerous accolades. [ 272 ] Following the release of his fourth studio album, Purpose , Bieber set major milestones globally. He became the first artist, since Elvis Presley in 2005, to replace his own song as number one on the UK Singles Chart . [ 273 ] He is the first artist in history to occupy the entire top thre',
