  ('cs_keith-jarrett_sec2', 'ent_keith-jarrett', 'narrative', 'Lawsuit against Steely Dan', 'Following the release of the album Gaucho in 1980 by the U.S. rock band Steely Dan , Jarrett sued the band for copyright infringement. Gaucho ''s title track, credited to Donald Fagen and Walter Becker , bore a resemblance to Jarrett''s "Long As You Know You''re Living Yours" from Jarrett''s 1974 album Belonging . In an interview with Musician magazine, Becker and Fagen were asked about the similarity between the two pieces of music, and Becker told Musician that he loved the Jarrett composition, while Fagen said they had been influenced by it. After their comments were published, Jarrett sued, and Becker and Fagen were legally obliged to add his name to the credits and provide Jarrett with publishing royalties. [ 49 ]',
   '["clm_wiki_keith-jarrett_sec2"]', '["src_wikidata"]',
   'general', 'en', 'assisted', 'kp-027-migration-0027', 'auto_approved', 1,
