  ('cs_kendrick-lamar_sec3', 'ent_kendrick-lamar', 'narrative', 'Public image', 'Lamar maintains a low public profile, [ 368 ] and is known to be reserved. He is reluctant to publicly discuss his personal life and generally avoids using social media . [ 369 ] [ 370 ] He is also decisive when engaging with mainstream media outlets, although journalists have complimented his " Zen -like" calmness and down to earth personality. [ 371 ] [ 372 ] According to Lamar, he has become "so invested in who I am outside of being famous, sometimes that''s all I know. I''ve always been a person that really didn''t dive too headfirst into wanting and needing attention. I mean, we all love attention, but for me, I don''t necessarily adore it." [ 373 ] His lyrics have been a topic of media scrutiny, leading to both praise and controversy. [ 13 ] [ 374 ] [ 375 ] Since the release of Good Kid, M.A.A.D City , some media outlets have described Lamar as the "modern hip hop messiah ". [ 376 ] Some critics dislike his "grating" political infusions, [ 377 ] causing him to be viewed as having a savior complex . [ 378 ] [ 379 ] He has previously likened himself to Nelson Mandela . [ 377 ] Lamar''s public perception has also been influenced by the various rap feuds he has been involved with. [ 380 ] [ 381 ] Although some journalists declared him the winner of his highly publicized conflict with Drake , [ 382 ] some felt that his victory was pyrrhic due to the severity of accusations introduced and the spread of online misinformation . [ 383 ] [ 384 ] Lamar has been praised for anti-racism activism, [ 385 ] but has also been labelled as exclusionary towards mixed-race individuals; [ 386 ] Michael Eric Dyson has called him a member of the "cults of pure identity that police the boundaries of Blackness like a rogue and racist cop". [ 387 ] Lamar has also been praised for feminist activism, but criticised for collaborating with abusers of women. [ 388 ] [ 389 ] Some magazines have called " Humble " a feminist song, [ 390 ] although the University of Melbourne ''s Lauren Rosewarn',
