  ('cs_ketanji-brown-jackson_sec2', 'ent_ketanji-brown-jackson', 'narrative', 'United States Sentencing Commission (2010–2014)', 'On July 23, 2009, President Obama nominated Jackson as vice chair of the United States Sentencing Commission . [ 33 ] [ 34 ] The Senate Judiciary Committee favorably reported her nomination by voice vote on November 5, 2009. The Senate confirmed her nomination by voice vote on February 11, 2010. [ 35 ] She succeeded Michael E. Horowitz , who had served from 2003 until 2009. Jackson served on the Sentencing Commission until 2014. [ 36 ] [ 27 ] During her time on the commission, it retroactively amended the sentencing guidelines to reduce the guideline range for crack cocaine offenses, [ 37 ] and enacted the "drugs minus two" amendment, which implemented a two offense-level reduction for drug crimes. [ 38 ]',
