  ('cs_kobe-bryant_sec3', 'ent_kobe-bryant', 'narrative', 'Player profile', 'Bryant shoots a fadeaway over Shane Battier in 2009 Bryant was a shooting guard . He was listed at 6 feet 6 inches (1.98 m) and 212 pounds (96 kg) . [ 286 ] He exhibited a high pain threshold while playing through injuries. [ 287 ] [ 288 ] Offense Bryant was often cited as one of the NBA''s most prolific scorers. [ 289 ] [ 290 ] He drew frequent comparisons to Jordan, after whom Bryant modeled his playing. [ 291 ] [ 292 ] [ 293 ] Like Jordan, Bryant became most known for his fall-away jump shot . [ 294 ] Chris Ballard of Sports Illustrated described another of Bryant''s moves as the "jab step-and-pause" in which Bryant jabbed his non- pivot foot forward to let the defender relax but instead of bringing the jab foot back, Bryant pushed off of it and drove around his opponent to reach the basket. [ 295 ] Bryant learned post moves through individual coaching sessions from Hakeem Olajuwon . [ 296 ] Bryant established a reputation for his shots in the closing moments of tight games, [ 297 ] [ 298 ] [ 299 ] even when double or triple-teamed, [ 300 ] and was noted as one of the premier closers in the NBA. [ 300 ] [ 301 ] In a 2012 annual survey of NBA general managers, Bryant was selected for the 10th consecutive season as the player general managers would want to take a clutch shot with a game on the line. [ 302 ] [ 303 ] Bryant''s willingness to take difficult shots drew criticism. [ 293 ] [ 304 ] Throughout his career, Bryant was disparaged as a selfish, high-volume shooter; [ 303 ] [ 305 ] [ 306 ] he missed more shots than any other player (LeBron James passed him in 2024). [ h ] Phil Jackson stated that Bryant "tends to force the action, especially when the game isn''t going his way. When his shot is off, Kobe will pound away relentlessly until his luck turns." [ 308 ] According to Bryant, "I would go 0 for 30 before I would go 0 for 9; 0 for 9 means you beat yourself, you psyched yourself out of the game." [ 309 ] Defense In addition to his offense, Bryant also estab',
   '["clm_wiki_kobe-bryant_sec3"]', '["src_wikidata"]',
   'general', 'en', 'assisted', 'kp-027-migration-0027', 'auto_approved', 1,
   80, unixepoch(), 'wikipedia', 391);
UPDATE content_section SET body_markdown = 'Kurt Donald Cobain was an American musician and songwriter. He was the lead vocalist, guitarist, primary songwriter, and a founding member of the grunge band Nirvana. Through his angsty songwriting and anti-establishment persona, he widened the thematic conventions of mainstream rock music. He was heralded as a spokesman of Generation X, and is widely recognized as one of the most influential musicians in the history of rock music.', word_count = 68, last_verified_at = unixepoch() WHERE id = 'cs_kurt-cobain_intro';
