  ('cs_larry-sanger_sec1', 'ent_larry-sanger', 'narrative', 'Nupedia and Wikipedia', '.mw-parser-output .hatnote{font-style:italic}.mw-parser-output div.hatnote{padding-left:1.6em;margin-bottom:0.5em}.mw-parser-output .hatnote i{font-style:normal}.mw-parser-output .hatnote+span.mw-empty-elt+.hatnote,.mw-parser-output .hatnote+link+.hatnote{margin-top:-0.5em}@media print{body.ns-0 .mw-parser-output .hatnote{display:none!important}} Main article: History of Wikipedia Sanger (seated, right) among the Bomis staff in mid-2000 Nupedia was a web-based encyclopedia whose articles were written by volunteer contributors possessing relevant subject matter expertise and reviewed by editors prior to publication, and were licensed as free content . [ 29 ] It was conceived by Jimmy Wales and underwritten by his company Bomis . [ 30 ] Wales had interacted with Sanger on mailing lists. [ 31 ] In January 2000, Sanger had e-mailed Wales and others about a potential "cultural news blog" project that would cover social and political issues that he had in mind after January 1, 2000, had passed and rendered his Y2K site obsolete. Wales replied with "Instead of doing that, why don''t you come and work on this idea that I''ve had?", presented the idea of Nupedia to Sanger, and invited him to join the project. [ 21 ] [ 28 ] Sanger was hired as Nupedia''s editor-in-chief. [ 30 ] He began to oversee Nupedia in February 2000, [ 32 ] developing a review process for articles and recruiting editors. [ 33 ] Through working on Nupedia, Sanger "found that it was a fascinating problem to organize people online to create encyclopedias". [ 34 ] Articles were reviewed through Nupedia''s email system before being posted on the site. [ 35 ] Nupedia made very slow progress and was at a standstill at the end of 2000, causing consternation to Sanger and Wales, [ 36 ] with Sanger saying that "by the summer of 2000, it had become clear that the process we tested out [for making articles on Nupedia] was very slow." [ 21 ] In January 2001, Sanger proposed the creation of a wiki to speed article de',
   '["clm_wiki_larry-sanger_sec1"]', '["src_wikidata"]',
   'general', 'en', 'assisted', 'kp-027-migration-0027', 'auto_approved', 1,
   80, unixepoch(), 'wikipedia', 302);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO content_section
  (id, entity_id, section_type, heading, body_markdown, claim_ids, source_ids,
