  ('cs_lebron-james_sec2', 'ent_lebron-james', 'career', 'Professional career', 'Cleveland Cavaliers (2003–2010) 2003–2004: Rookie of the Year The Cleveland Cavaliers selected James as the first overall pick of the 2003 NBA draft . [ 41 ] James chose jersey number 23 in honor of Michael Jordan . [ 42 ] In his first regular season game, James scored 25 points in a 106–92 loss to the Sacramento Kings , setting an NBA record for the most points scored by a prep-to-pro player in his debut performance. [ 43 ] At the conclusion of the 2003–04 season , James became the first Cavalier to receive the NBA Rookie of the Year Award . [ 44 ] and only the third player in league history to average at least 20 points, five rebounds, and five assists per game as a rookie. [ 45 ] 2004–2008: Rise to superstardom In the 2004–05 season , James earned his first NBA All-Star Game selection, contributing 13 points, 8 rebounds, and 6 assists in a winning effort for the Eastern Conference . [ 46 ] Teams took note of his rapid development, and Denver Nuggets coach George Karl told Sports Illustrated : "It''s weird talking about a 20-year-old kid being a great player, but he is a great player ... He''s the exception to almost every rule." [ 47 ] On March 20, James scored 56 points against the Toronto Raptors , setting Cleveland''s new single-game points record. [ 48 ] At the end of the season, James was named to his first All-NBA Team . [ 35 ] [ 48 ] The Cavaliers again failed to make the playoffs, finishing the season 42–40. [ 49 ] During the 2006 offseason, James signed a three-year, $60 million contract extension with the Cavaliers, with the option for a fourth year. [ 50 ] At the 2006 All-Star Game , James led the Eastern Conference to victory with 29 points and was named the NBA All-Star Game Most Valuable Player (MVP). [ 51 ] He finished second in overall NBA MVP Award voting, behind Steve Nash . [ 52 ] Under James''s leadership, the Cavaliers qualified for the playoffs for the first time since 1998. [ 53 ] In his postseason debut, James recorded a triple-double in a',
