  ('cs_lebron-james_sec3', 'ent_lebron-james', 'career', 'National team career', 'James attempting a shot over China''s Yao Ming at the 2008 Summer Olympics As a 19-year-old rookie, James made his debut for the United States national team at the 2004 Olympics in Athens, Greece, although he spent most of the event on the bench. [ 403 ] [ 404 ] Team USA finished with a bronze medal, becoming the first U.S. basketball team to return home without a gold medal since the NBA started allowing active players to participate in the Olympics. [ 405 ] James felt he was not given "a fair opportunity to play". [ 404 ] At the 2006 FIBA World Championship in Japan, James took on a greater role for Team USA, averaging 13.9 points, 4.8 rebounds, and 4.1 assists per game as co-captain. [ 406 ] [ 407 ] The team finished the tournament with an 8–1 record, winning another bronze medal. [ 406 ] During this time, James was known for his disrespectful attitude toward the national team''s staff, coaches and players. While assembling the 2008 Olympic squad , Team USA managing director Jerry Colangelo and coach Mike Krzyzewski told James he could only play if he improved his attitude, and James complied. Colangelo said that James matured significantly as both a player and a person as a result of the ultimatum. [ ah ] At the FIBA Americas Championship 2007 , James put up 31 points against Argentina in the championship game, the most ever by an American in an Olympic qualifier. [ 411 ] Team USA went 10–0, winning the championship and qualifying for the 2008 Olympics in Beijing , [ 403 ] where they went undefeated and won the gold medal. [ 412 ] [ 413 ] James attempting a dunk at the 2012 Summer Olympics James did not play at the 2010 FIBA World Championship but became the leader of Team USA ahead of the 2012 Olympics in London. [ 414 ] [ 415 ] During a game against Australia , he recorded the first triple-double in U.S. Olympic basketball history with 11 points, 14 rebounds, and 12 assists. [ ai ] Team USA won the gold medal, again defeating Spain in the final game. [ 417 ] J',
   '["clm_wiki_lebron-james_sec3"]', '["src_wikidata"]',
   'general', 'en', 'assisted', 'kp-027-migration-0027', 'auto_approved', 1,
