  ('cs_linus-torvalds_sec1', 'ent_linus-torvalds', 'narrative', 'Authority and trademark', 'As of 2006, approximately 2% of the Linux kernel was written by Torvalds. [ 29 ] Despite the thousands who have contributed to it, his percentage is still one of the largest. However, he said in 2012 that his own personal contribution is now mostly merging code written by others, with little programming. [ 54 ] He retains the highest authority to decide which new code is incorporated into the standard Linux kernel. [ 55 ] Torvalds holds the Linux trademark [ 56 ] and monitors its use, [ 57 ] chiefly through the Linux Mark Institute .',
