  ('cs_lizzo_sec3', 'ent_lizzo', 'narrative', 'Artistry', 'Lizzo''s music incorporates a variety of genres, including pop , [ 149 ] [ 150 ] [ 151 ] [ 152 ] hip-hop , [ 153 ] [ 154 ] funk-pop , [ 154 ] R&B , [ 152 ] and soul . [ 154 ] Lizzo''s influences include Missy Elliott , [ 155 ] Lauryn Hill , [ 156 ] and Beyoncé . [ 157 ] Primarily starting as a rapper, Lizzo incorporated singing into her debut record. She stated in an interview in 2018, "I was always afraid of being a singer, but then when I heard Lauryn Hill, I was like, maybe I can do both", adding that her debut album was inspired by The Miseducation of Lauryn Hill , and Hill''s "rapping, singing, being political." [ 156 ] She has cited Diana Ross as a fashion reference. [ 158 ] In an article for The Guardian in 2019, writer Leonie Cooper credited Lizzo for "the woodwind renaissance" as "the flute''s brightest champion" in the mainstream. [ 159 ]',
